            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "WH Harris"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good and very simple! Everyone loved it. It looked like a little too much mayo as I was doing it so I cut back to about 2/3 cups. Also mix the cream cheese and the mayo before everything else, really helps you to eliminate the lumps of cream cheese throughout."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Linda Farrell"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made today for a party that I thought was my b-day party, it was. Used 8oz cream cheese, 1/2-3/4c miracle whip. Put in microwave for about 15 seconds and mashed with a fork to remove lumps and clumps. Added 10oz can RoTel, 11ozs green giant mexicorn and 2 green peppers sliced. Topped with 1/4c. shredded cheddar cheese. It's really not too ugly but it sure is great! Will definately make again and again!!! Served with Fritos Scoops and all I brought home was the emply bowl. My brother didn't even know it had corn in it (haha).",
            "datePublished": "2010-08-21T17:54:20.213Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jan Richards"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Even though the cream cheese was soft, there were still globs - better to mix the cream cheese with the mayo first and then add the tomatoes and corn. I reduced the mayo to 2/3 cup. I also added sliced black olives. Everyone loved it!",
            "datePublished": "2009-07-05T09:10:32.747Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Hannah's Mom"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My family literally scraped the bowl clean! I used half a cup of mayo and half a cup of sour cream along with the cream cheese, used 1 can of rotel and added 1 1/2 tablespoons of diced jalapeños. I also added a packet of taco seasoning and it was to die for!!!",
            "datePublished": "2019-09-19T00:43:50.150Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mary Disselhoff"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! Used 1/2 cup of light mayo, and fire-roasted Rotel (Great Value brand) and an extra green onion. Easy to put together. I did mix the cream cheese and mayo and stuck in the microwave to blend it easier. Better chilled. You could add stuff like shrimp to this!",
            "datePublished": "2025-02-23T01:52:13.688Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Stephanie Gray"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I found this recipe several years ago and have made it many times. Everyone always loves it and asks for the recipe. My alterations: I always use 2 packages of cream cheese, and only add 3 or 4 spoonfuls of mayo, otherwise the mayo is too overbearing for our liking. I also add a chopped jalapeno for an extra kick. I have added the green jalapeno pepper tabasco sauce in the past also, and we enjoyed that as well. I think it tastes best when chilled a couple hours. Also, make sure the cream cheese is totally softened, and mix the mayo &amp; cream cheese together before adding the other ingredients.",
            "datePublished": "2015-12-26T11:41:27.857Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
